Z||000004||Black88GT||10-06-2000||09:58 PM||||The moment he told me he was willing to trade for the '84 I would have jumped all over it.  Do the carfax thing just to be sure, but its worth that in parts easily.<BR>Where is it located? <P>||||reg||3
Z||000005||Fformula88||10-06-2000||10:26 PM||||Sounds like a super buy.  Almost too good.  As long as everything checks out... good mechanicals, no signs of obvious colision damage etc etc I'd say jump all over it.  Thats way too cheap for a Formula with 51K.  Just be careful 'cause with that milage it should be going for a lot more.  Especially if he's willing to trade it for an 84 with more milage.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||AkursedX||10-06-2000||10:33 PM||||I'd be a little cautious and suspicious about that price.  It sounds a little fishy to me.  Just make sure to check everything you possibly can and make sure to test drive it and give it a good run-around before buying it.<BR>But hey, if it all checks out, then you got yourself quite a deal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000007||88formula||10-06-2000||10:56 PM||||Do a tittle search on it to make sure it was never in an accident. Mine was a mint 50,000 mile car and I paid $3900 for it last year. Back then the book value was $4300. It sounds too good to be true and usaully is. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||KnightRyder31||10-07-2000||05:18 PM||||It does have some slight body damage, I would replace the hood and front left fender...but thats it. Its not that bad.<BR>Its in Michigan.||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||10-08-2000||12:41 PM||||That's how my 88 coupe was when I bought it. I had to replace what was left over of the fender, hood, windshield, door. <BR>Be sure to check out the upper control arm. Also, with the car jacked up on the hit side, grab the wheel and jerk it side to side. If there's play you may have to replace a tie rod. On my Fiero I had to replace both the upper control arm and inner tie rod, and pull the frame out a few inches. Wasn't fun but worth the $350 for the car!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||10-08-2000||01:58 PM||||I bought an 88 Formula a couple of weeks ago. Good condition and running. No bad body parts but can use paint. Only problem is the shifter cables (hopefully). I paid $500 for it.<P>It seems that a Fiero is worth exactly what someone is willing to pay for it. I have seen 84s go for a couple thousand and 88s go for a few hundred. There doesn't seem to be any rule to it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||10-09-2000||12:32 PM||||If its just the body that needs repair... GET IT NOW!!!!  Finding a Formula with those miles is a real steel.<P>Songman is exactly right... a Fiero or any used car for that matter is only worth what someone is willing to pay for it.  My bought my Formula for $2850 in 1996.  It was in mint condition inside and out except for its spoiler was missing, and a couple cigarette burn holes in the drivers seat.  The trunk lid had been repaired (holes filled in) and painted, but otherwise the car was perfect.  It had 67,9000 miles.  I thought it was a really good price at the time (book value was almost $6000), so I jumped on it!  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000012||william_thorniii||10-09-2000||12:46 PM||||Knight,<P>Keep us posted on this car... like Mike and Archie before me... I would be interested in this vehicle if you are not.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||10-09-2000||12:46 PM||||<B>Go for it!</B>  I wouldn't trade your '84 if you don't have to, use that for everyday driving.  Hey you can't have too many anyway.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'd be concerned if the spaceframe got kinked but sounds like this is just cosmetic damage anyway, maybe something to check into.<P>I'm from MI also, I could probably check it out for you too.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> j/k<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">            <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-09-2000).]||||reg||14
